  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing CSS Animations**\n\nOkay, I\'m now digging into `src/index.css` to figure out the specific CSS and animations required. I\'ve re-read the user\'s instructions for the thematic animation. I\'m focusing on crafting an elegant vector animation using SVG and pure CSS with `@keyframes`.\n\n\n**Designing Animated Logistics**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design phase, focusing on creating a visually clear representation of the logistics flow. I\'m prioritizing SVG and pure CSS, as requested. The route path is defined, and I\'m experimenting with animated `stroke-dashoffset` for the dashed line effect. I\'m also exploring motion along the path for a truck or telemetry icon, considering `offset-path` as a candidate for smooth movement.\n\n\n**Defining Path Animations**\n\nI\'ve defined the waypoint nodes, and the most recent focus has been designing a vehicle glyph that travels smoothly between them. I\'m leaning toward using `offset-path` for this, aiming for a clean and efficient animation. Telemetry cards will float alongside the path, displaying key data points like \"Carga despachada,\" \"Previs\303\243o no prazo,\" and other real-time data with visual indicators. I\'m also confirming the dark UI aesthetic, using the specified color palette and considering fine borders to enhance the clean look.\n\n\n**Refining Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the interactive simulator widget. I\'ve defined the input fields for origin/destination CEPs, weight, and dimensions. I\'m also implementing the \"Calcular op\303\247\303\265es de envio\" button with a subtle calculating state. The visual design is progressing, aiming for clean mathematical spacing and high-contrast button styles. I\'m prioritizing the single vibrant green action accent for primary conversions and the neutral secondary buttons. I\'m using sentence case for all labels.\n\n\n**Developing Shipment Tracking**\n\nI\'m now integrating the shipment tracking widget, focusing on the input for the tracking code and the \"Consultar\" button. I am thinking through the live shipment telemetry preview, which will display status, last update, trajectory, and driver details. I\'m taking ideas from Sinka\'s tabs, organizing the content for shippers and carriers. I\'m working with a 4-card grid for our solutions and differentiators.\n\n\n**Implementing B2B Onboarding**\n\nI\'m working on the \"Seja um parceiro\" section, creating a dedicated B2B onboarding card with a registration form. It includes fields for the company name, CNPJ, type of operation, and corporate email, all leading to a \"Cadastrar empresa / parceiro\" CTA. I\'m also planning the success confirmation feedback. I\'m checking the CSS to add custom utility animations and typography rules if needed.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 227219323
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
