    thinking: "**Designing the Widget**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the Freight Simulator widget design. I envision a visually engaging central card demonstrating easy simulation. Key input fields will include \"Origin Zip Code,\" \"Destination Zip Code,\" and \"Weight,\" ensuring user-friendliness.\n\n\n**Refining the Interface**\n\nI\'ve been refining the Freight Simulator widget\'s interface. Now I am including fields for \"Approximate Weight (kg)\" and \"Dimensions (L x W x H).\" A \"Calculate Shipping Options\" button will trigger a display of carrier options. The UI guidelines are strict: a clean aesthetic with no dot grids, fake security badges, all-caps text, generic icons, or flashy gradients. The color palette will be based on zinc tones, with a vibrant green action button.\n\n\n**Detailing the Simulation**\n\nI\'m now detailing the simulation\'s interactive fidelity.  I\'ve defined form fields with clean default values. Upon clicking \"Calcular op\303\247\303\265es de envio,\" a brief but authentic calculation state will appear, followed by live comparison options. The three carrier result cards are now defined, including specific transportadoras, modalities, estimated delivery times, SLAs, pricing, and \"Contratar frete\" buttons, with badges \"Melhor Pre\303\247o\", \"Mais R\303\241pido\", and \"Opera\303\247\303\243o Direta.\"\n\n\n"
