  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Landing Page Refactor**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt, specifically the requirements for refactoring the landing page. It\'s clear the focus needs to be on adhering to a new prompt that emphasizes a minimalist design system. I\'m prioritizing understanding the specifics of those requirements to create a robust plan.\n\n\n**Defining LogiFlow Landing Page**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining the scope and core features for LogiFlow\'s landing page. The focus is on the \"Intelligent Freight Quote\" functionality \342\200\223 automatic volume calculation, comparing carrier tables. The constraints are shaping the minimalist design focus, and avoiding complex logic, with the final code being a single HTML file with Tailwind CSS and native CSS for micro-interactions. My plan is to ensure it aligns with our React setup seamlessly.\n\n\n**Clarifying Anti-AI-Slop Directives**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the specific \"Anti-AI-Slop\" directives. It is critical I grasp the prohibited elements, such as GPS tracking displays, any mention of real-time telemetry, and inflated metrics in the Hero section. My design approach must avoid dot grids, cheesy seals, and ALL-CAPS labels. I\'m focusing on the \"Clean-UI\" identity, with a zinc/slate dark theme and vibrant emerald for action points. Also the proper redirects for the landing page are now set, like \"Simular Frete\", \"Seja um Parceiro\" and \"Acessar Sistema\".\n\n\n**Structuring Landing Page Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing the landing page sections. The header will feature a minimalist logo and clear navigation links, with prominent CTAs for system access and registration. The Hero section will showcase the core value proposition with a compelling headline and subtitle. Rather than a GPS map, I\'m visualizing a mockup demonstrating the freight comparison feature, highlighting automatic cubage and carrier options. The three-step \"How It Works\" storytelling will be next, followed by an interactive freight simulator widget and a section for both carriers and shippers.\n\n\n"
