  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Vision**\n\nMy focus is now on meticulously analyzing the requirements. I\'m carefully considering the transition to a light mode design, drawing inspiration from platforms such as Stripe, Linear, and Sinka. I\'m aiming for a luminous, clean, and modern aesthetic for the landing page.\n\n\n**Defining the Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the visual identity. The plan is a luminous base with a pure white background and soft gray transition sections. Typography will be high-contrast black/lead for prominence and a softer gray for body text. The accent color will be a vibrant, warm amber for key buttons, tactile details, and highlights, ensuring it is agile and inviting without being overwhelming. The design prohibits dark modes and clich\303\251d styling elements.\n\n\n**Refining the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now completely focused on refining the Hero Section. It needs to be 100% centered and clean \342\200\223 no heavy forms or intrusive elements. I\'m avoiding ALL-CAPS text and focusing on sentence case for the entire interface. The header will be minimalist, with a white background and subtle blur on scroll, featuring a geometric logo and focused navigation.\n\n\n**Crafting the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the hero section copy. I\'ve centered a subtitle promoting the core value proposition. Primary and secondary action buttons are now styled, aiming to provide clear calls to action. The primary button has a dynamic look, inviting quick freight simulations, while the secondary targets transport partner onboarding.\n\n\n**Developing the Simulator**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the simulator section. I\'m crafting a clean, welcoming block with a narrative invitation: \"Ready to find the best freight for your shipment?\" I\'m emphasizing instant calculations, and highlighting the competitive quote system. The main call to action is a bright, amber-toned button encouraging users to simulate a freight. I am also planning the partners section in a grid format.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Light Mode**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the light mode implementation. I\'ve updated the `index.html` to remove the dark mode classes and added the light mode classes. In `src/index.css`, I\'m working on typography and adjusting styles. My current focus is refining components, especially the `Navbar.tsx` and `Hero.tsx`. I\'m transitioning these to the desired visual style.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 648914683
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
